{"title": "Motorola is filling the gap OnePlus left behind, mostly", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/01/motorola-oneplus-gap/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-1_942c71.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">As we near the launch of Motorola’s return to the flagship space, it’s becoming clear that the company is ready to fill a gap left by the departure of OnePlus, though there’s one very obvious difference between the two.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left wp-block-paragraph\"><em>9to5Google Weekender by Ben Schoon is a part of our free newsletter that also includes ‘Inbox,’ a twice-weekly roundup of key stories from around the web by Daniel Bader. <a href=\"https://9to5google.beehiiv.com/subscribe\">Sign up here</a> to get Weekender delivered to your inbox every Sunday along with ‘Inbox’ on Tuesday and Thursday. <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/feature/newsletter/\">You can find past issues here</a>.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/01/motorola-oneplus-gap/#more-734888\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-01T05:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-02T20:09:31.608480+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Motorola Signature 27 specs detailed in new video, including Tandem OLED display", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/10/31/motorola-signature-27-specs-hands-on/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/10/motorola-signature-27-hands-on-2.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Ahead of its launch next week, a new video offers a closer look at the Motorola Signature 27 as well as confirming some key specs.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/10/31/motorola-signature-27-specs-hands-on/#more-735267\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-10-31T03:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-02T20:09:31.608480+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Samsung mercilessly mocks iPhone Duo ‘crackgate’ in Galaxy Z Fold 8 ads [Video]", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/10/30/samsung-mocks-iphone-duo-crackgate-galaxy-z-fold-8/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/10/galaxy-z-fold-8-iphone-duo-crackgate.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Samsung isn’t holding back when it comes to the iPhone Duo’s messy start. In new ads, the company mocks iPhone Duo’s “crackgate” with a push for customers to buy the Galaxy Z Fold 8 instead, and there’s not an ounce of subtlety here.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/10/30/samsung-mocks-iphone-duo-crackgate-galaxy-z-fold-8/#more-735274\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-10-30T16:20:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-02T20:09:31.608480+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
